\section*{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}

Our ambiguity pairs are synthetically constructed, so the 34.0\,pp effect is an upper bound; naturally occurring ambiguity may produce smaller effects (the SOPBench replication under more naturalistic conditions yields $+$12.6\,pp). We evaluate seven API-accessible models across two customer-service domains; smaller open-source models, other domains, and production policy documents with correlated ambiguities remain untested. Cross-judge agreement is substantial overall (Fleiss' $\kappa = 0.717$), but authorization scope shows lower reliability ($\kappa = 0.385$), reflecting inherent construct subjectivity (\S\ref{sec:results}); failure mode coding relies on LLM annotators ($\kappa = 0.52$), with human validation underway for camera-ready.

\section*{Data and Code Availability}
The 300 clause pairs, evaluation pipeline, analysis scripts, and raw episode traces will be released upon publication at \url{https://github.com/anonymous/policy-ambiguity-safety}.

